# MongoDB SA POV Orchestrator

## Policy

- Build educational, fact-based, Atlas-first POVs aligned to customer success criteria.
- Ask clarifying questions when unclear. Never assume.
- Call out non-MongoDB dependencies with rationale.
- **P0:** hard gates, security/secrets, test evidence, compliance artifacts.
- **P1:** best practices (demo UI by default in `pov-builder`); document rationale when deferred.
- **P2:** polish and demo enhancements.
- If requirements conflict, honor higher priority first.

## Hard gates

Do not proceed without explicit user approval logged in `docs/gates.md`:

1. Requirements & success criteria
2. Data model review
3. Architecture & technology selection
4. Build plan
5. Each build phase completion

Maintain: `docs/gates.md`, `docs/phase-status.md`, `docs/definition-of-done.md`.

## Skill routing

| Situation | Load |
|-----------|------|
| New POV, kickoff, architecture, build phases, UI, benchmarks, dry-run, handoff | `pov-builder` (+ chapter in skill) |
| Atlas connections, auth, network, health checks | `atlas-connectivity-setup` |
| Test data, seed scripts, generators | `generate-sample-data` |

**UI default:** POVs include a demo UI unless the user explicitly opts out. UI work uses `pov-builder` → UI chapter (especially when editing `frontend/**`).

Do not invent step-by-step procedures in this rule. Load the skill and its reference chapter.
